window.I18N=window.I18N||{};I18N.en={"ui":{"skip":"Skip to the catalogue","a11y":"Accessibility","a11y_text":"Text size","a11y_normal":"Normal text","a11y_big":"Large text","a11y_bigger":"Extra large text","a11y_theme":"Theme","theme_auto":"Automatic","theme_light":"Light","theme_dark":"Dark","a11y_contrast":"High contrast","a11y_motion":"Reduce motion","a11y_links":"Underline links and buttons","cart":"Order","lang":"Language","lede":"Chillies from the collection, hottest to mildest: how hot they are, how they smell, where they come from and which dishes they suit.","st_var":"varieties","st_fotos":"photographs","st_paises":"countries","st_arom":"very aromatic","presets_t":"Quick picks","pr_peixe":"Fish and seafood","pr_perfume":"Big aroma, little fire","pr_rechear":"For stuffing","pr_secar":"Powder and flakes","pr_ferm":"Fermented sauces","pr_super":"Superhots","filters":"Filter","search_label":"Search","search_ph":"Search name, ingredient, dish…","f_heat":"Heat","f_aroma":"Aroma","f_perfil":"Aroma profile","f_meal":"Course","f_prep":"Preparation","f_country":"Origin","f_species":"Species","f_photo":"Only with a photo","clear":"Clear filters","show_n":"Show {n} varieties","no_country":"No country given","other_species":"Other / to be confirmed","views":"Views","tab_cards":"Varieties","tab_map":"Map","tab_chart":"Heat × aroma","sort":"Sort","sort_desc":"Hottest first","sort_asc":"Mildest first","sort_aroma":"Most aromatic first","sort_name":"Name (A–Z)","count":"{n} of {t} varieties","remove_filter":"Remove filter: {f}","search_tag":"Search: “{q}”","photo_tag":"With a photo","empty":"No varieties match these filters.","no_photo":"no photo","no_photo_long":"No photograph yet","open_card":"Open card for {name}","photos_n":"{n} photos","h0":"Sweet","h1":"Mild","h2":"Medium","h3":"Hot","h4":"Very hot","h5":"Extreme","hx0":"Bell pepper","hx1":"Biquinho, banana pepper","hx2":"Jalapeño, Bishop Crown","hx3":"Rocoto, ajís, bird's eye","hx4":"Habanero, Scotch Bonnet","hx5":"Bhut Jolokia, Reaper","a1":"Subtle","a2":"Aromatic","a3":"Very aromatic","ad1":"Green or vegetal notes; little perfume.","ad2":"Fruit or citrus present without dominating.","ad3":"Intense tropical or floral perfume. Adds aroma even in small amounts.","aroma_label":"Aroma","heat_label":"Heat","no_data":"No data","no_value":"No numeric value","profile_none":"Profile not described","t_referência":"reference","t_vendedor":"seller","t_estimativa":"estimate","t_sem dados":"no data","b_variedade":"Published description of the variety.","b_variedade-base":"Description of the base variety (this colour or selection has none of its own).","b_grupo":"Description of the group it belongs to.","b_pais":"Inferred from the parents of the cross.","b_espécie":"No description of the variety; classified by species.","b_sem dados":"No data.","sp_unknown":"Species to be confirmed","d_kitchen":"In the kitchen","d_meals":"Courses","d_pair":"Pairs with","d_prep":"Preparations","d_flavor":"Flavour and aroma","d_look":"Appearance","d_origin":"Origin","d_alts":"Alternatives in the collection","d_sources":"Sources","close":"Close","flag_alt":"Flag: {c}","map_title":"Where the varieties come from","map_help":"Tap a country or a circle to see its chillies, from hottest to mildest. The ring shows the heat levels of each country's varieties. Drag to move; use + and −, two fingers or Ctrl + mouse wheel to zoom.","map_none":"{n} without a country: collectors' crosses, unpublished origin or variety still to be identified.","map_empty":"No varieties with a known origin in the current filters.","map_aria":"World map with the number of varieties per country of origin","chart_help":"Each dot is a variety, placed at the typical value of its Scoville range (logarithmic scale). Tap a dot to open its card.","by_aroma":"By aroma","by_species":"By species","var_short":"var.","chart_aria":"Varieties on the Scoville scale","guide_t":"How to read the catalogue","g_heat":"Heat","g_aroma":"Aroma","g_tech":"Technique","g_heat_p":"Each value is marked as <b>reference</b> (published range), <b>seller</b> (whoever bred or sells the seed; rarely lab-tested), <b>estimate</b> (inferred from the parents, the base variety or the group) or <b>no data</b>.","g_aroma_p":"The catalogue's own classification, grounded in research: <i>C. chinense</i> is the species richest in esters and terpenes, with fruity, exotic aromas; <i>C. baccatum</i> and <i>C. pubescens</i> lean earthy and vegetal (rocoto smells of cucumber); <i>C. annuum</i> mixes fruity and green notes. Where a published description of the variety exists, it takes precedence; otherwise the species is used and the card says so.","tip1":"<b>Fresh or dried.</b> Drying lowers the intensity and complexity of the aroma; terpenes drop by more than 90%. For perfume, use fresh; for smoke and depth, dried or smoked.","tip2":"<b>Controlling the heat.</b> Capsaicin sits mostly in the white placenta: removing it cuts the heat a lot. Roasting softens it; so does boiling rocoto.","tip3":"<b>Whole, then removed.</b> In a stew, a whole superhot (stem off) taken out at the end gives flavour with little burn.","tip4":"<b>Superhots (level 5).</b> Gloves, goggles, and grind outdoors. A pinch is enough for a whole pot.","sources_t":"Sources","updated":"Updated {d}.","disclaimer":"Values and descriptions gathered from the sources listed; those marked as estimate or no data should be confirmed. Real heat varies with sun, watering and ripeness.","add":"Add","add_order":"Add to order","update_order":"Update order","in_cart":"In order · {q}","added":"{name}: {q} seeds in your order","unavailable":"No seeds available","qty":"Quantity","seeds":"seeds","less":"Fewer","more":"More","o_title":"Order request","o_empty":"You haven't chosen any seeds yet. Use “Add” on the catalogue cards.","o_seeds":"Chosen seeds","o_remove":"Remove","o_total":"{n} varieties · {q} seeds","o_data":"Order details","f_name":"Full name","f_email":"Email","f_phone":"Phone","f_addr":"Address","f_zip":"Postcode","f_city":"Town / city","f_ctry":"Country","f_nif":"Tax number (optional, for the invoice)","f_delivery":"Delivery","del_post":"Send by post","del_pickup":"Collect in person","f_notes":"Notes","f_notes_ph":"E.g. timing, acceptable alternatives, questions…","f_consent":"I agree that this data is used only to handle this order.","o_privacy":"The request is emailed to Jorge Santos through the FormSubmit service. There is no payment on the site: price and postage are confirmed by email.","o_send":"Send request","o_sending":"Sending…","o_ok_t":"Request sent","o_ok":"Reference {ref}. You will get an email reply confirming the order, price and postage.","o_fail_t":"The request could not be sent automatically","o_fail":"You can send the same request from your own email program, or copy it and paste it into a message to {email}.","o_activation":"Automatic sending is not active yet (the FormSubmit activation email still needs confirming). Please send the request from your email.","o_mail":"Send from my email","o_copy":"Copy request","o_copied":"Request copied","o_back":"Back to the catalogue","o_req":"Required field","o_bad_email":"Enter a valid email","o_need_items":"Add at least one variety.","o_need_consent":"You need to agree before sending.","o_fix":"Some fields need correcting.","o_ref":"Reference","o_req_mark":"required","show_n_1":"Show 1 variety","o_total_1":"1 variety · {q} seeds","credit":"Seeds, growing and identification:","ig":" on Instagram","title":"CHILLI CATALOGUE","title_html":"<span>CHILLI</span> CATALOGUE","pg_pratos":"Dishes","pg_molhos":"Sauces and preparations","pg_mundo":"World cuisines","pg_outras":"More suggestions","pr_carne":"Meat","pr_aves":"Poultry","pr_saladas":"Salads and raw dishes","pr_sopas":"Soups, stews and fish stews","pr_massas":"Rice, pasta and pizza","pr_petiscos":"Snacks and starters","pr_veg":"Vegetarian","pr_doces":"Sweets and chocolate","pr_mpicante":"Hot sauce","pr_salsa":"Fresh salsa","pr_piri":"Piri-piri and chilli oil","pr_marinada":"Marinades","pr_conserva":"Preserves and pickles","pr_geleia":"Jellies and jams","pr_fumado":"Smoked","pr_mx":"Mexico","pr_pe":"Peru and the Andes","pr_car":"Caribbean","pr_br":"Brazil","pr_asia":"Asia","pr_africa":"Africa","pr_na":"North America","f_trad":"Culinary tradition","chef_t":"For the kitchen","chef_force":"Strength (by weight)","chef_force_v":"≈ {x}× a jalapeño","chef_force_0":"No heat","chef_force_note":"Based on the typical SHU value (jalapeño = 2,500–10,000).","chef_equiv":"Market chilli with similar heat","chef_trad":"Culinary tradition","chef_safety":"Handling","safe_low":"Normal handling.","safe3":"Wash your hands after cutting and keep away from your eyes.","safe4":"Wear gloves to cut and keep away from your eyes.","safe5":"Gloves, goggles and good ventilation; grind outdoors. Not suitable for children.","safe_unk":"No heat data: taste a small amount first.","mk_bell":"Bell pepper","mk_cayenne":"Cayenne","mk_name":"Chilli","mk_x":"Strength","g_market":"Market equivalents","g_market_p":"Values from the Wikipedia Scoville table; strength based on the typical value of each range.","health_t":"Health and safety","health_intro":"The studies concern chilli and capsaicin in general, not individual varieties. General information, not a substitute for medical advice.","health_levels":"Precautions by heat level","h_mort":"<b>Regular consumption.</b> In a meta-analysis of 4 cohort studies (564,748 people), eating chilli regularly, compared with rarely or never, was associated with 13% lower all-cause mortality, 11% lower cardiovascular mortality and 8% lower cancer mortality. These are associations: they do not prove that chilli is the cause.","h_nutr":"<b>Nutrition.</b> 100 g of raw red chilli contain about 40 kcal and 144 mg of vitamin C. Cooking uses only a few grams, so the real contribution is small.","h_met":"<b>Metabolism.</b> In a meta-analysis of 9 trials, capsaicin increased energy expenditure by about 59 kcal a day, and only in people with overweight. Another review describes the effect as small.","h_med":"<b>Medicine.</b> A patch with 8% capsaicin has been authorised in the European Union since 2009 to treat peripheral neuropathic pain in adults. It is a medicine, not a food.","h_dig":"<b>Digestion.</b> Spicy food is among the usual triggers of heartburn and acid reflux; the NHS advises people with these symptoms to avoid what triggers them.","h_skin":"<b>Skin and eyes.</b> Chilli oil irritates skin and eyes: wash your hands after cutting and take care around your eyes. With the hottest ones, wear gloves.","h_hot":"<b>Superhots.</b> Eating very hot chillies can cause stomach pain, vomiting and, in some cases, hospital admission. In 2018 a case was described of a man with sudden headaches and temporary narrowing of brain arteries after eating a Carolina Reaper in a contest; he recovered.","map_tools":"Map controls","map_zin":"Zoom in","map_zout":"Zoom out","map_reset":"Show the whole world","map_keys":"With the keyboard: arrows to move, + and − to zoom in or out, 0 to show the whole world. Tab moves through the countries.","map_back":"Back to the list of countries","map_filter":"Show only these in Varieties","map_n":"{n} varieties","map_n_1":"1 variety","map_zero":"No varieties from this country with the current filters.","nav":"Navigation","nav_cards":"Varieties","nav_map":"Map","nav_chart":"Chart","nav_guide":"Guide","dev":"Developed by","ai_note":"Note: this website was developed with the help of artificial intelligence.","tab_id":"Identify","nav_id":"Identify","id_t":"Identify from a photo","id_help":"Photograph the whole fruit, on its own and well lit, on a smooth, neutral surface (light worktop, white board, plate). The fruit should fill a good part of the picture.","id_cam":"Take a photo","id_gal":"Choose from gallery","id_privacy":"The photo never leaves your device: it is analysed in the browser and is neither stored nor sent.","id_note":"Experimental. Compares the colour and shape of the fruit with the {n} photos in the catalogue. Many varieties look alike and the same one changes colour as it ripens, so the result is a suggestion: always check the card. Varieties without a photo are not included.","id_working":"Analysing…","id_res":"Closest matches","id_sim":"similarity","id_show":"Show these in the catalogue","id_warn":"The fruit could not be separated well from the background. Try a smooth, neutral surface, with the fruit filling a good part of the picture.","id_err":"This image could not be read.","id_prev":"Area analysed (the rest was treated as background)","id_tag":"Identification: {n} suggestions","id_empty":"No photo yet. Results will appear here.","cur_t":"Curiosities","c_old":"<b>6,100 years.</b> Chilli starch grains that old have been found at archaeological sites from the Bahamas to Peru.","c_art":"<b>Artefacts.</b> Vessels from Chiapas, Mexico, around 2,400 years old still hold capsaicin residues.","c_name":"<b>Journey.</b> In the 16th century, the Portuguese took chillies to Africa and Asia, including Goa.","c_birds":"<b>Birds.</b> They don't feel the heat: they eat the fruit and spread the seeds intact.","c_scov":"<b>Scoville.</b> The scale was born in 1912 and measured heat with human tasters.","c_nobel":"<b>Nobel 2021.</b> Capsaicin helped David Julius discover TRPV1, the receptor for heat and pain.","pr_more":"More suggestions","pr_groups":"Suggestion groups","cur_prev":"Previous curiosity","cur_next":"Next curiosity","cur_pause":"Pause curiosities","cur_play":"Resume curiosities","cur_pos":"Curiosity {i} of {n}","cur_dot":"Show curiosity {i}","care_t":"Precautions","care_hand":"Handling","care_prec":"When eating","hand_low":"No special care; wash your hands after cutting.","hand_2":"Wash your hands after cutting and avoid touching your eyes.","hand_3":"Wash your hands well after cutting; do not touch your eyes or contact lenses.","hand_4":"Wear gloves to cut; wash the board and knife straight afterwards; do not touch your eyes.","hand_5":"Gloves and goggles; cut, grind or dry with good ventilation or outdoors; wash board, knife and grinder straight afterwards.","hand_unk":"No heat data: wear gloves until you have tasted it.","prec_low":"Low heat: suitable for most people.","prec_2":"Moderate heat; people with heartburn or reflux should taste with care.","prec_3":"Add a little at a time and taste; people with heartburn or reflux should use little.","prec_4":"Use in small amounts and tell your guests; not advised for children or for people with heartburn or reflux.","prec_5":"A pinch is enough for a whole dish. Not suitable for children. In quantity it can cause stomach pain and vomiting; serious cases have been described with superhots.","prec_unk":"Taste a very small amount first.","map_legend":"Heat level in the ring","id_cta_aria":"Identify a chilli from a photo","cur_kick":"Did you know…","cur_photo":"Pictured: {name}","ribbon_t":"From mildest to hottest","ribbon_lo":"mild","ribbon_hi":"extreme","unid":"To be identified","lang_err":"This language could not be loaded. Reload the page and try again.","c_vitc":"<b>Vitamin C.</b> In 1932, Szent-Györgyi extracted it in bulk from Szeged paprika. Nobel Prize in 1937.","c_plac":"<b>Where it burns.</b> Capsaicin sits in the white placenta that holds the seeds, not in the seeds.","c_milk":"<b>Against the burn.</b> In a 2019 study, milk brought more relief than water, soft drinks or alcohol-free beer.","c_rec":"<b>Record.</b> Since 2023, Guinness lists Pepper X as the hottest: 2.69 million SHU on average.","c_sp5":"<b>Five species.</b> Mostly <i>C. annuum</i>, <i>C. baccatum</i>, <i>C. chinense</i>, <i>C. frutescens</i> and <i>C. pubescens</i> are grown.","c_chin":"<b>Misleading name.</b> In 1776, Jacquin named it <i>C. chinense</i> (\"from China\"), but the species is American."},"txt":{"Peixe e marisco":"Fish and seafood","Sopas e estufados":"Soups and stews","Molhos e condimentos":"Sauces and condiments","Fresco":"Fresh","Molho picante":"Hot sauce","Conserva":"Preserves","Seco / pó":"Dried / powder","Ornamental":"Ornamental","Caranguejo":"Crab","Ostras":"Oysters","Peixe branco":"White fish","Natas":"Cream","Vegetal":"Vegetal","Arroz, massas e pizza":"Rice, pasta and pizza","Carnes":"Meat","Marinada":"Marinade","Salsa":"Salsa","Peixe":"Fish","Feijão":"Beans","Alho":"Garlic","Cebola":"Onion","Orégãos":"Oregano","Coentros":"Coriander","Tropical":"Tropical","Floral":"Floral","Fermentado":"Fermented","Manga":"Mango","Ananás":"Pineapple","Lima":"Lime","Mel":"Honey","Tomate":"Tomato","Frutado doce":"Sweet fruit","Azeite picante":"Chilli oil","Leite de coco":"Coconut milk","Chocolate negro":"Dark chocolate","Aves":"Poultry","Maracujá":"Passion fruit","Cebola roxa":"Red onion","Porco":"Pork","Frango":"Chicken","Doces e sobremesas":"Desserts and sweets","Geleia":"Jelly","Fumado":"Smoked","Damasco":"Apricot","Passas":"Raisins","Cacau":"Cocoa","Carne de vaca":"Beef","Terroso / fumado":"Earthy / smoky","Peixe seco ou fermentado":"Dried or fermented fish","Salteados e wok":"Stir-fries and wok","Cítrico":"Citrus","Petiscos":"Snacks and starters","Saladas e crus":"Salads and raw","Recheado":"Stuffed","Queijo":"Cheese","Bacon":"Bacon","Abacate":"Avocado","Pimento":"Bell pepper","Tucupi":"Tucupi","Vegetariano":"Vegetarian","Queijo feta":"Feta cheese","Azeitonas":"Olives","Salsicha":"Sausage","Queijos curados":"Cured cheeses","Vinagre":"Vinegar","Carne picada":"Minced meat","Queijo fresco":"Fresh cheese","Batata":"Potato","Chalota":"Shallot","Cabrito":"Kid goat","Camarão":"Prawns","Arroz":"Rice","Queijo creme":"Cream cheese","Feta":"Feta","Presunto":"Cured ham","Marisco":"Shellfish","Citrinos":"Citrus fruit","Legumes":"Vegetables","Toranja":"Grapefruit","Manjericão":"Basil","Tomilho":"Thyme","Salsa (erva)":"Parsley","Feno-grego":"Fenugreek","Cardamomo":"Cardamom","Gengibre":"Ginger","Pimenta-da-jamaica":"Allspice","Vinho":"Wine","Fruta tropical":"Tropical fruit","Chocolate":"Chocolate","Herança (EUA)":"Heirloom (USA)","Pimenta-de-cheiro (Brasil)":"Pimenta-de-cheiro (Brazil)","Superhot (cruzamento)":"Superhot (cross)","Superhot":"Superhot","Habanero":"Habanero","Habanero / Scorpion?":"Habanero / Scorpion?","Superhot (Bhut / Ghost)":"Superhot (Bhut / Ghost)","Superhot (Ghost)":"Superhot (Ghost)","Jalapeño":"Jalapeño","Ají dulce":"Ají dulce","Pimenta amazónica":"Amazonian chilli","Cruzamento":"Cross","Pimento doce (F1)":"Sweet pepper (F1)","Suave":"Mild","Aji (experimental)":"Ají (experimental)","Rocoto":"Rocoto","Por confirmar":"To be confirmed","Superhot (7 Pot)":"Superhot (7 Pot)","Aji":"Ají","Bird's eye (tipo rawit)":"Bird's eye (rawit type)","Doce-picante":"Sweet-hot","Superhot (FOX)":"Superhot (FOX)","Pimenta roxa (Brasil)":"Purple chilli (Brazil)","Africana":"African","Aji amazónico":"Amazonian ají","Bird's eye":"Bird's eye","Pimenta silvestre":"Wild chilli","Pimenta-de-cheiro":"Pimenta-de-cheiro","C. frutescens / annuum?":"C. frutescens / annuum?","C. annuum (provável)":"C. annuum (probable)","C. annuum var. glabriusculum":"C. annuum var. glabriusculum","C. chinense (provável)":"C. chinense (probable)","Africana ocidental":"West African","Brasileira":"Brazilian","Caribenha":"Caribbean","Etíope":"Ethiopian","Indiana":"Indian","Indonésia":"Indonesian","Mexicana":"Mexican","Norte-americana":"North American","Peruana":"Peruvian","Sul-africana":"South African","Surinamesa":"Surinamese","Tailandesa":"Thai","Herança afro-americana dos EUA (Baltimore, Filadélfia, séc. XIX); a cultivar terá vindo das Caraíbas.":"African-American heirloom from the USA (Baltimore, Philadelphia, 19th century); the cultivar probably came from the Caribbean.","Fresco e vivo, a pimento, por vezes ligeiramente amargo, como jalapeño ou serrano.":"Fresh and bright, peppery, sometimes slightly bitter, like jalapeño or serrano.","Folhagem variegada verde e branca. Frutos estriados que passam de creme a vermelho.":"Variegated green and white foliage. Striped fruits that turn from cream to red.","Tradicional nas casas de marisco: sopa de caranguejo com natas, ostras. Colhida creme ou verde, tempera molhos brancos e cremes sem mudar a cor. Substitui jalapeño ou serrano.":"Traditional in seafood houses: cream of crab soup, oysters. Picked cream or green, it seasons white sauces and creams without changing their colour. A substitute for jalapeño or serrano.","Norte e Nordeste do Brasil.":"North and Northeast Brazil.","Sem valor publicado. 'Muito aroma e pouca ardência.'":"No published value. 'Lots of aroma, little heat.'","Muito aromática e pouco ardida: perfuma o prato sem o tornar picante.":"Very aromatic and barely hot: it perfumes a dish without making it spicy.","Frutos pequenos, vermelhos ou amarelos.":"Small fruits, red or yellow.","Usar fresca para perfumar feijão e feijoada, moqueca, caldeirada, arroz, carne e peixe. Sem sementes, o ardor quase desaparece. Molho simples: com alho, cebola, orégãos, vinagre e azeite.":"Use fresh to perfume beans and feijoada, moqueca, caldeirada, rice, meat and fish. Without the seeds the heat almost disappears. Simple sauce: with garlic, onion, oregano, vinegar and olive oil.","Cruzamento de colecionador: 7 Pot Jonah (Trindade e Tobago) × Pimenta da Neyde (Brasil).":"Collector's cross: 7 Pot Jonah (Trinidad and Tobago) × Pimenta da Neyde (Brazil).","Sem medição. Pais: 7 Pot Jonah 800.000–1.200.000; Pimenta da Neyde 150.000–250.000.":"Not measured. Parents: 7 Pot Jonah 800,000–1,200,000; Pimenta da Neyde 150,000–250,000.","A 7 Pot Jonah é frutada e doce; a Neyde é floral e ligeiramente amarga. O resultado varia por geração.":"7 Pot Jonah is fruity and sweet; Neyde is floral and slightly bitter. The result varies by generation.","Cruzamento entre a 7 Pot Jonah (rugosa, com ferrão) e a Pimenta da Neyde (roxa). A aparência varia de geração para geração.":"A cross between 7 Pot Jonah (wrinkled, with a stinger) and Pimenta da Neyde (purple). Appearance varies from generation to generation.","Usar em quantidades mínimas: molhos (de vinagre, doces ou fumados), pó para dosear à pitada, óleo picante. Tirar a placenta branca reduz o ardor; assar antes suaviza. Luvas e cuidado com os olhos.":"Use in tiny amounts: sauces (vinegar-based, sweet or smoky), powder to dose by the pinch, chilli oil. Removing the white placenta reduces the heat; roasting first softens it. Gloves, and mind your eyes.","Variante de cor da Carolina Reaper (Ed Currie, Carolina do Sul, EUA).":"Colour variant of the Carolina Reaper (Ed Currie, South Carolina, USA).","Reaper vermelha: 1.400.000–2.200.000; média certificada 1.641.183. A cor bordô não tem medição própria.":"Red Reaper: 1,400,000–2,200,000; certified average 1,641,183. The burgundy colour has no measurement of its own.","Por baixo do ardor, doce e algo frutada (Reaper vermelha).":"Under the heat, sweet and somewhat fruity (red Reaper).","Rugosa, com cauda em gancho. Cor bordô.":"Wrinkled, with a hooked tail. Burgundy colour.","Sobretudo molhos picantes; a fruta combina com molhos de vinagre, doces ou fumados. Seca, ganha fumo e doçura; uma pitada substitui caiena. Não comer crua. Tirar a placenta branca reduz o ardor. Luvas, óculos e máscara ao manipular.":"Mainly hot sauces; the fruit suits vinegar-based, sweet or smoky sauces. Dried, it gains smoke and sweetness; a pinch replaces cayenne. Do not eat raw. Removing the white placenta reduces the heat. Gloves, goggles and a mask when handling.","Ed Currie, Carolina do Sul (EUA). Recordista Guinness até 2023, quando foi ultrapassada pela Pepper X.":"Ed Currie, South Carolina (USA). Guinness record holder until 2023, when it was overtaken by Pepper X.","1.400.000–2.200.000 (PepperScale); a tabela da Wikipedia indica 1.500.000–2.500.000. Média certificada pela Guinness (2017): 1.641.183.":"1,400,000–2,200,000 (PepperScale); the Wikipedia table gives 1,500,000–2,500,000. Average certified by Guinness (2017): 1,641,183.","Doce e algo frutada por baixo do ardor.":"Sweet and somewhat fruity under the heat.","Vermelha, rugosa, com cauda em gancho.":"Red, wrinkled, with a hooked tail.","Troy Primeaux (EUA): Naga Morich × 7 Pod Douglah.":"Troy Primeaux (USA): Naga Morich × 7 Pod Douglah.","Mais de 1.000.000 (indicação do vendedor).":"Over 1,000,000 (seller's figure).","Doce e frutada, depois ardor intenso e longo.":"Sweet and fruity, then intense, long-lasting heat.","Castanho-escuro, retorcida e rugosa, cerca de 6 × 2–2,5 cm.":"Dark brown, twisted and wrinkled, about 6 × 2–2.5 cm.","Molhos picantes e pó muito forte. A Douglah, um dos pais, dá-se bem em sopas e chilis terrosos. Usar em quantidades mínimas: molhos (de vinagre, doces ou fumados), pó para dosear à pitada, óleo picante. Tirar a placenta branca reduz o ardor; assar antes suaviza. Luvas e cuidado com os olhos.":"Hot sauces and very strong powder. Douglah, one of the parents, works well in earthy soups and chillies. Use in tiny amounts: sauces (vinegar-based, sweet or smoky), powder to dose by the pinch, chilli oil. Removing the white placenta reduces the heat; roasting first softens it. Gloves, and mind your eyes.","Seleção de habanero vermelho feita na Califórnia (EUA).":"Selection of red habanero made in California (USA).","Aroma floral típico de habanero.":"Floral aroma typical of habanero.","Lanterna vermelha, enrugada.":"Red lantern, wrinkled.","Molhos de fruta (manga, ananás, maracujá), marinadas de porco e frango, salsas. Na cozinha do Iucatão o habanero usa-se inteiro, em puré ou em salsa.":"Fruit sauces (mango, pineapple, passion fruit), marinades for pork and chicken, salsas. In Yucatán cooking the habanero is used whole, puréed or in salsa.","Fica no limite entre 'muito picante' e 'extremo' (350.000–750.000).":"Sits on the line between 'very hot' and 'extreme' (350,000–750,000).","Habanero laranja liso":"Smooth orange habanero","Amazónia; hoje sobretudo Península do Iucatão (México). O nome vem de Havana (Cuba), onde era muito comerciado.":"Amazon; today mainly the Yucatán Peninsula (Mexico). The name comes from Havana (Cuba), where it was widely traded.","Aroma floral e fruta tropical. Os habaneros laranja e castanhos têm composição aromática mais rica que os vermelhos (Pino et al., citado por Garruti et al.).":"Floral aroma and tropical fruit. Orange and brown habaneros have a richer aroma composition than red ones (Pino et al., cited by Garruti et al.).","Lanterna laranja, pele lisa.":"Orange lantern, smooth skin.","Salsas, molho de manga ou ananás, marinadas, ceviche em dose mínima, compotas e geleias picantes.":"Salsas, mango or pineapple sauce, marinades, ceviche in a tiny dose, hot jams and jellies.","Habanero laranja/amarelo":"Orange/yellow habanero","Amazónia; hoje sobretudo Península do Iucatão (México).":"Amazon; today mainly the Yucatán Peninsula (Mexico).","Aroma floral e fruta tropical.":"Floral aroma and tropical fruit.","Lanterna laranja a amarela.":"Orange to yellow lantern.","Molho de manga ou ananás, marinadas, compota picante, piri-piri em azeite.":"Mango or pineapple sauce, marinades, hot jam, piri-piri in olive oil.","Habanero chocolate liso":"Smooth chocolate habanero","Caraíbas (as fontes não indicam país).":"Caribbean (sources give no country).","425.000–577.000 (habanero chocolate).":"425,000–577,000 (chocolate habanero).","Doçura frutada de habanero com notas terrosas e fumadas.":"Habanero's fruity sweetness with earthy and smoky notes.","Castanho-chocolate, liso.":"Chocolate brown, smooth.","Mole e salsas escuras e terrosas; rubs para carnes, como alternativa mais picante ao chipotle; molhos picantes.":"Mole and dark, earthy salsas; rubs for meat, as a hotter alternative to chipotle; hot sauces.","Habanero chocolate rugoso (Scorpion?)":"Wrinkled chocolate habanero (Scorpion?)","Caraíbas (se for habanero chocolate).":"Caribbean (if it is a chocolate habanero).","Habanero chocolate: 425.000–577.000. Se for Trinidad Scorpion chocolate: 750.000–1.500.000.":"Chocolate habanero: 425,000–577,000. If it is a chocolate Trinidad Scorpion: 750,000–1,500,000.","Doçura frutada com notas terrosas e fumadas.":"Fruity sweetness with earthy and smoky notes.","Castanho-chocolate, pele rugosa.":"Chocolate brown, wrinkled skin.","Mole e salsas escuras; rubs para carnes; molhos picantes. Provar com cuidado antes de usar.":"Mole and dark salsas; rubs for meat; hot sauces. Taste carefully before using.","Se for um Trinidad Scorpion chocolate e não um habanero, o picante sobe para o nível extremo (750.000–1.500.000).":"If it is a chocolate Trinidad Scorpion rather than a habanero, the heat rises to the extreme level (750,000–1,500,000).","Seleção escura da Bhut Jolokia (Nordeste da Índia).":"Dark selection of Bhut Jolokia (Northeast India).","Bhut Jolokia: 855.000–1.041.427 (medições publicadas). Sem dados sobre a seleção 'Black Diamond'.":"Bhut Jolokia: 855,000–1,041,427 (published measurements). No data on the 'Black Diamond' selection.","As ghost são doces e frutadas, com fundo fumado; as variantes escuras/chocolate são mais ricas e fumadas.":"Ghost peppers are sweet and fruity with a smoky background; dark/chocolate variants are richer and smokier.","Alongada, rugosa, pele fina, de cor escura.":"Elongated, wrinkled, thin-skinned, dark coloured.","Tradição do Nordeste da Índia: caris, pickles e chutneys, com porco ou peixe seco/fermentado. Fresca ou seca, um pedaço chega para um prato inteiro. Assar antes suaviza.":"Tradition of Northeast India: curries, pickles and chutneys, with pork or dried/fermented fish. Fresh or dried, one piece is enough for a whole dish. Roasting first softens it.","Nordeste da Índia (Assam, Nagaland, Manipur). Também chamada naga jolokia, raja mirchi ou ghost pepper.":"Northeast India (Assam, Nagaland, Manipur). Also called naga jolokia, raja mirchi or ghost pepper.","855.000–1.041.427 (medições publicadas). Recorde Guinness em 2007.":"855,000–1,041,427 (published measurements). Guinness record in 2007.","Doce e frutada, com fundo fumado. O ardor demora uns segundos a chegar e dura muito.":"Sweet and fruity with a smoky background. The heat takes a few seconds to arrive and lasts a long time.","Vermelha, alongada (6–8 cm), rugosa, pele fina.":"Red, elongated (6–8 cm), wrinkled, thin-skinned.","Tradição do Nordeste da Índia: caris, pickles e chutneys, com porco ou peixe seco/fermentado. Também em molhos de churrasco e salsas. Um pedaço seco chega para um prato inteiro; assar antes suaviza.":"Tradition of Northeast India: curries, pickles and chutneys, with pork or dried/fermented fish. Also in barbecue sauces and salsas. One dried piece is enough for a whole dish; roasting first softens it.","Purple Ghost × Trinidad Butch T Scorpion.":"Purple Ghost × Trinidad Butch T Scorpion.","Purple Ghost Scorpion: 600.000–800.000+ (vendedor). Variante branca sem dados próprios.":"Purple Ghost Scorpion: 600,000–800,000+ (seller). White variant has no data of its own.","Como a ghost, com fundo doce e frutado. As ghost brancas tendem a ser menos frutadas.":"Like the ghost, with a sweet, fruity background. White ghosts tend to be less fruity.","Variante branca/creme de uma linha que costuma ser vermelha com riscas roxas.":"White/cream variant of a line that is usually red with purple streaks.","Molho picante, salsa em doses mínimas, pó forte.":"Hot sauce, salsa in tiny doses, strong powder.","Enrico Lai (Itália).":"Enrico Lai (Italy).","Classificada como superhot pelo vendedor; sem valor publicado.":"Classed as a superhot by the seller; no published value.","Ácida e suculenta, aroma de habanero.":"Tangy and juicy, with a habanero aroma.","Paredes grossas e textura rugosa. Existe em várias cores (Pink/Peach, Purple, Orange, White).":"Thick walls and a rough texture. Comes in several colours (Pink/Peach, Purple, Orange, White).","Salsas e salteados, em quantidades mínimas, pela fruta e pelo ardor; molhos.":"Salsas and stir-fries, in tiny amounts, for the fruit and the heat; sauces.","Linha Jay's (Jay Weaver, Pensilvânia, EUA): ghost × Trinidad Scorpion, cruzamento acidental. Esta é a variante branca.":"Jay's line (Jay Weaver, Pennsylvania, USA): ghost × Trinidad Scorpion, an accidental cross. This is the white variant.","Jay's Peach Ghost Scorpion: ~1.000.000. A branca não tem medição própria.":"Jay's Peach Ghost Scorpion: ~1,000,000. The white has no measurement of its own.","Família Jay's: frutada e ligeiramente floral. As ghost brancas tendem a ser menos frutadas.":"Jay's family: fruity and slightly floral. White ghosts tend to be less fruity.","Branca/creme quando madura, rugosa.":"White/cream when ripe, wrinkled.","Por ser clara, serve para molhos claros que não devem mudar de cor (maionese picante, molho de alho), em gotas; também pó.":"Being pale, it suits light sauces that should not change colour (spicy mayonnaise, garlic sauce), by the drop; also powder.","Selecionada a partir de fenótipos de Gator Jigsaw (Michael Christensen, EUA).":"Selected from Gator Jigsaw phenotypes (Michael Christensen, USA).","'Muito picante' segundo o vendedor; sem valor publicado.":"'Very hot' according to the seller; no published value.","Sem descrição publicada. A Gator Jigsaw, de onde vem, é descrita como terrosa.":"No published description. Gator Jigsaw, which it comes from, is described as earthy.","Vermelha e rugosa. Muito produtiva.":"Red and wrinkled. Very productive.","Muito produtiva: boa para fazer molho fermentado ou pó em quantidade. Usar em quantidades mínimas: molhos (de vinagre, doces ou fumados), pó para dosear à pitada, óleo picante. Tirar a placenta branca reduz o ardor; assar antes suaviza. Luvas e cuidado com os olhos.":"Very productive: good for making fermented sauce or powder in quantity. Use in tiny amounts: sauces (vinegar-based, sweet or smoky), powder to dose by the pinch, chilli oil. Removing the white placenta reduces the heat; roasting first softens it. Gloves, and mind your eyes.","Jalapeño variegado, selecionado de uma planta encontrada numa estufa comercial. O jalapeño é do México.":"Variegated jalapeño, selected from a plant found in a commercial greenhouse. Jalapeño is from Mexico.","Jalapeño: 2.500–10.000. Descrito como suave e ligeiramente doce.":"Jalapeño: 2,500–10,000. Described as mild and slightly sweet.","Suave e ligeiramente doce.":"Mild and slightly sweet.","Folhagem variegada. Frutos creme com riscas verdes que amadurecem até vermelho.":"Variegated foliage. Cream fruits with green stripes that ripen to red.","Como jalapeño: salsas, petiscos, pickles, poppers recheados. A folhagem branca e verde torna a planta muito decorativa.":"Like jalapeño: salsas, snacks, pickles, stuffed poppers. The white and green foliage makes the plant very decorative.","Caraíbas.":"Caribbean.","Cachucha: 0–1.000. O nome 'Fairytale' não está confirmado.":"Cachucha: 0–1,000. The name 'Fairytale' is not confirmed.","Doce e frutada, notas de erva e fumo: aroma de habanero quase sem ardor.":"Sweet and fruity, with herbal and smoky notes: habanero aroma with almost no heat.","Achatada e enrugada, parecida com habanero, mas doce.":"Flattened and wrinkled, like a habanero, but sweet.","Base do sofrito caribenho (com pimento, tomate, cebola, alho e coentros). Assada em sopas, estufados, arroz, feijão e carnes; crua em saladas e salsas.":"Base of Caribbean sofrito (with bell pepper, tomato, onion, garlic and coriander). Roasted in soups, stews, rice, beans and meat; raw in salads and salsas.","Os dados são da Cachucha; o nome 'Fairytale' não está confirmado. O fruto fotografado é rosa-arroxeado, cor que as fontes não descrevem para a Cachucha.":"The data are for Cachucha; the name 'Fairytale' is not confirmed. The photographed fruit is pinkish-purple, a colour the sources do not describe for the Cachucha.","Amazónia brasileira (Amazonas e Pará).":"Brazilian Amazon (Amazonas and Pará).","Sem valor SHU publicado.":"No published SHU value.","Sem descrição de sabor nas fontes consultadas.":"No flavour description in the sources consulted.","Fina e comprida (3–9 cm), em forma de 'minhoca'. Planta escura, fruto laranja.":"Long and thin (3–9 cm), 'worm'-shaped. Dark plant, orange fruit.","Na Amazónia vende-se fresca ou em molho caseiro e entra no tucupi, servido em pratos como o tacacá. Também em geleias, doces e condimentos.":"In the Amazon it is sold fresh or as a homemade sauce and goes into tucupi, served in dishes such as tacacá. Also in jellies, sweets and condiments.","Cruzamento de colecionador; os dois pais são brasileiros.":"Collector's cross; both parents are Brazilian.","Imprevisível: Biquinho 500–1.000 × Neyde 150.000–250.000.":"Unpredictable: Biquinho 500–1,000 × Neyde 150,000–250,000.","Depende do fenótipo.":"Depends on the phenotype.","Espera-se forma de bico com pigmentação roxa, mas varia.":"Expected to be beak-shaped with purple pigmentation, but it varies.","Provar antes de usar. Se sair suave, conserva como a biquinho; se sair picante, molhos.":"Taste before using. If it comes out mild, pickle it like biquinho; if hot, use in sauces.","Descoberta no Brasil: ghost (Bhut Jolokia) × Pimenta da Neyde.":"Discovered in Brazil: ghost (Bhut Jolokia) × Pimenta da Neyde.","1.100.000+ (estimativa publicada).":"1,100,000+ (published estimate).","Como a ghost: frutada com um toque floral.":"Like the ghost: fruity with a floral touch.","Quase preta antes de amadurecer; madura fica vermelho-escuro ou laranja. Pequena e atarracada (5–7 cm).":"Almost black before ripening; ripe it turns dark red or orange. Small and stocky (5–7 cm).","Molhos e salsas muito diluídos. Pouco produtiva; vale também pela planta, muito decorativa.":"Sauces and salsas, heavily diluted. Low yield; also worth growing for the very decorative plant.","Híbrido F1 comercial.":"Commercial F1 hybrid.","0 (doce).":"0 (sweet).","Doce, para comer como snack.":"Sweet, for snacking.","Frutos com riscas de cor.":"Fruits with coloured stripes.","Cru em saladas e petiscos, grelhado, recheado.":"Raw in salads and snacks, grilled, stuffed.","Seleção de habanero; as fontes não indicam a origem.":"Habanero selection; sources give no origin.","Classe habanero: 100.000–350.000.":"Habanero class: 100,000–350,000.","Aroma floral e frutado típico dos habaneros.":"Floral, fruity aroma typical of habaneros.","Cor mostarda quando madura, forma de lanterna.":"Mustard colour when ripe, lantern-shaped.","Molhos de fruta, marinadas, compotas picantes.":"Fruit sauces, marinades, hot jams.","Cultivar de horta comum. As variantes picantes chamam-se Hungarian wax.":"Common garden cultivar. The hot variants are called Hungarian wax.","Suave e ácida; fica mais doce ao amadurecer.":"Mild and tangy; gets sweeter as it ripens.","Comprida, amarelo-banana, lisa.":"Long, banana-yellow, smooth.","Em pickle às rodelas para pizza, sanduíches e salada grega; recheada em antipasto ou servida quente com salsicha italiana e queijos; em relish, salsa e geleia.":"Pickled in rings for pizza, sandwiches and Greek salad; stuffed on antipasti or served warm with Italian sausage and cheeses; in relish, salsa and jelly.","Cruzamento experimental de C. baccatum.":"Experimental C. baccatum cross.","Sem valor publicado; o vendedor diz que o picante é variável.":"No published value; the seller says the heat is variable.","Varia com a maturação e o sol.":"Varies with ripeness and sun.","Laranja, por vezes com riscas vermelhas.":"Orange, sometimes with red stripes.","Fresca, em saladas, pickles, salsa, molhos, pó e secagem. O vendedor sugere um molho fresco com pimento doce, cebola, alho, vinagre e pouca malagueta.":"Fresh, in salads, pickles, salsa, sauces, powder and drying. The seller suggests a fresh sauce with sweet pepper, onion, garlic, vinegar and a little chilli.","Andes (Peru, Bolívia, Equador). Seleção compacta e produtiva.":"Andes (Peru, Bolivia, Ecuador). Compact, productive selection.","Os rocotos variam muito: 30.000–100.000 (PepperScale) e 50.000–250.000 (Wikipedia); alguns estudos dão valores mais baixos. Descrito como acima da média.":"Rocotos vary a lot: 30,000–100,000 (PepperScale) and 50,000–250,000 (Wikipedia); some studies give lower values. Described as above average.","Carne grossa e sumarenta; aroma a pepino e a pimento.":"Thick, juicy flesh; aroma of cucumber and bell pepper.","Pequeno, parece uma azeitona verde. Amadurece para verde-mostarda. Sementes pretas.":"Small, looks like a green olive. Ripens to mustard green. Black seeds.","Rocoto relleno (Arequipa, Peru): cozido, recheado com carne picada, cebola e alho, coberto com queijo e levado ao forno. Também em creme com queijo fresco, pasta com óleo, salsa crua com cebola e lima, ou molho verde (ají de huacatay) com batata. Ferver reduz o picante. Tem muita água e seca mal.":"Rocoto relleno (Arequipa, Peru): boiled, stuffed with minced meat, onion and garlic, topped with cheese and baked. Also in a cream with fresh cheese, a paste with oil, a raw salsa with onion and lime, or a green sauce (ají de huacatay) with potatoes. Boiling reduces the heat. It holds a lot of water and dries poorly.","Rocoto Amarelo (Ericeira)":"Yellow rocoto (Ericeira)","Andes (Peru, Bolívia, Equador). Lote: Ericeira.":"Andes (Peru, Bolivia, Ecuador). Seed lot: Ericeira.","Os rocotos variam muito: 30.000–100.000 (PepperScale) e 50.000–250.000 (Wikipedia); alguns estudos dão valores mais baixos.":"Rocotos vary a lot: 30,000–100,000 (PepperScale) and 50,000–250,000 (Wikipedia); some studies give lower values.","Amarelo, carnudo, sementes pretas. Folhas peludas e flores roxas.":"Yellow, fleshy, black seeds. Hairy leaves and purple flowers.","Rocoto vermelho (Ericeira)":"Red rocoto (Ericeira)","Vermelho, carnudo, sementes pretas.":"Red, fleshy, black seeds.","Andes (Peru, Bolívia, Equador). Lote: 'Booth'.":"Andes (Peru, Bolivia, Ecuador). Seed lot: 'Booth'.","Carnudo, sementes pretas.":"Fleshy, black seeds.","Rocoto castanho (Ericeira)":"Brown rocoto (Ericeira)","Castanho, carnudo, sementes pretas.":"Brown, fleshy, black seeds.","Rocoto vermelho (Califórnia)":"Red rocoto (California)","Andes (Peru, Bolívia, Equador). Lote: Califórnia.":"Andes (Peru, Bolivia, Ecuador). Seed lot: California.","Jalapeño (México; o nome vem de Xalapa, Veracruz). Lote 'Darth'.":"Jalapeño (Mexico; the name comes from Xalapa, Veracruz). Seed lot 'Darth'.","Jalapeño: 2.500–10.000.":"Jalapeño: 2,500–10,000.","Notas verdes e vegetais; maduro e vermelho é mais picante que verde.":"Green, vegetal notes; ripe and red it is hotter than green.","Jalapeño de cor escura.":"Dark-coloured jalapeño.","Poppers recheados com queijo (panados ou com bacon), pickle às rodelas para nachos, pico de gallo e salsas. Maduro e fumado chama-se chipotle. Também em geleia, bebidas, pho, bánh mì e pizza.":"Poppers stuffed with cheese (breaded or wrapped in bacon), pickled rings for nachos, pico de gallo and salsas. Ripe and smoked it is called chipotle. Also in jelly, drinks, pho, bánh mì and pizza.","Big Red (Áustria)":"Big Red (Austria)","Lote da Áustria.":"Seed lot from Austria.","Sem dados.":"No data.","Variedade por identificar.":"Variety still to be identified.","Variante de cor da Carolina Reaper.":"Colour variant of the Carolina Reaper.","Reaper vermelha: 1.400.000–2.200.000. Esta cor não tem medição própria.":"Red Reaper: 1,400,000–2,200,000. This colour has no measurement of its own.","Frutada e doce, ardor que cresce.":"Fruity and sweet, with building heat.","Rugosa, com cauda. Cor rosa-pêssego.":"Wrinkled, with a tail. Pink-peach colour.","Rugosa, com cauda. Cor pêssego.":"Wrinkled, with a tail. Peach colour.","Cruzamento: Pimenta da Neyde (Brasil) × 7 Pot Douglah (Trindade e Tobago).":"Cross: Pimenta da Neyde (Brazil) × 7 Pot Douglah (Trinidad and Tobago).","Sem medição. Pais: Neyde 150.000–250.000; 7 Pot Douglah 923.889–1.853.986.":"Not measured. Parents: Neyde 150,000–250,000; 7 Pot Douglah 923,889–1,853,986.","A Douglah é frutada, terrosa e com notas de noz.":"Douglah is fruity, earthy and nutty.","Espera-se cor escura (roxo a chocolate). Varia por geração.":"Expected to be dark (purple to chocolate). Varies by generation.","Molhos e pó em doses mínimas; a Douglah dá-se bem em sopas e chilis terrosos.":"Sauces and powder in tiny doses; Douglah works well in earthy soups and chillies.","Família 7 Pot (originária de Trindade e Tobago); criador desta linha desconhecido.":"7 Pot family (from Trinidad and Tobago); breeder of this line unknown.","Sem dados próprios. As 7 Pot andam na ordem de 800.000–1.850.000.":"No data of its own. 7 Pots are in the range of 800,000–1,850,000.","As 7 Pot são frutadas.":"7 Pots are fruity.","Cor mostarda, rugosa tipo 7 Pot.":"Mustard colour, wrinkled, 7 Pot type.","Provavelmente América do Sul; no Brasil chama-se cambuci e terá sido levada para a Europa pelos portugueses. Cultivada também em Barbados.":"Probably South America; in Brazil it is called cambuci and was probably taken to Europe by the Portuguese. Also grown in Barbados.","As abas são doces; o picante está no centro.":"The wings are sweet; the heat is in the centre.","Forma de coroa ou disco voador, com 3–4 abas. Verde-claro, madura vermelha.":"Shaped like a crown or flying saucer, with 3–4 wings. Light green, red when ripe.","Carne fina e estaladiça. As abas, cortadas, servem cruas quase sem picante em saladas; inteira recheada; pickles.":"Thin, crisp flesh. The wings, cut off, can be served raw almost without heat in salads; whole for stuffing; pickles.","Híbrido da casa Drax (Itália).":"Hybrid from the Drax house (Italy).","Cerca de 1.900.000 (indicação do vendedor).":"About 1,900,000 (seller's figure).","Diz-se que o ardor é mais forte e mais longo que o da Reaper.":"Said to burn harder and longer than the Reaper.","Sem descrição publicada.":"No published description.","Linha Big Mama (Troy Primeaux, EUA).":"Big Mama line (Troy Primeaux, USA).","Big Yellow Mama: 750.000–1.000.000 (vendedor). Creme: sem dados.":"Big Yellow Mama: 750,000–1,000,000 (seller). Cream: no data.","As amarelas são citrinas e frutadas.":"The yellow ones are citrusy and fruity.","Linha Big Mama: 5–7 cm, pele lisa ou rugosa.":"Big Mama line: 5–7 cm, smooth or wrinkled skin.","Molhos picantes e marinadas, em doses mínimas.":"Hot sauces and marinades, in tiny doses.","Pode corresponder à Big Yellow Mama.":"May correspond to Big Yellow Mama.","Peru.":"Peru.","Doce, com nota de maçã.":"Sweet, with a note of apple.","Pequenos, cónicos, eretos. Amarelo-claro, depois roxo, laranja e por fim vermelho.":"Small, conical, upright. Pale yellow, then purple, orange and finally red.","Cozinhar, ou secar e moer em pó. Planta muito decorativa.":"Cook with it, or dry and grind into powder. Very decorative plant.","Na fotografia: amarelo-alaranjada, alongada e rugosa.":"In the photograph: yellow-orange, elongated and wrinkled.","Sem referências publicadas com este nome.":"No published references under this name.","Suriname, onde é a pimenta nacional.":"Suriname, where it is the national chilli.","Frutada, com notas de manga e ananás; ligeiramente doce.":"Fruity, with notes of mango and pineapple; slightly sweet.","Irregular, enrugada, tipo sino, um pouco maior que a Scotch Bonnet. Amarelo vivo, por vezes laranja.":"Irregular, wrinkled, bell-like, a little larger than Scotch Bonnet. Bright yellow, sometimes orange.","Usada em quase toda a cozinha do Suriname. Molhos, marinadas, salsas; muito boa com frango e peixe; também fresca ou seca.":"Used in almost all Surinamese cooking. Sauces, marinades, salsas; excellent with chicken and fish; also fresh or dried.","Desconhecida.":"Unknown.","Condor's Beak: 'muito picante', ao nível de habanero (vendedor). Branca: sem dados.":"Condor's Beak: 'very hot', at habanero level (seller). White: no data.","Semelhante a habanero.":"Similar to habanero.","Condor's Beak: alongada, pontiaguda, pendente (~5 cm). A cor normal vai de verde a roxo e vermelho; esta é a variante branca.":"Condor's Beak: elongated, pointed, pendant (~5 cm). The usual colour goes from green to purple and red; this is the white variant.","Molhos picantes; decorativa.":"Hot sauces; decorative.","Cajamarca é uma região do Peru.":"Cajamarca is a region of Peru.","Sem dados próprios. Os ajis costumam ter 30.000–50.000.":"No data of its own. Ajís are usually 30,000–50,000.","Os ajis são frutados.":"Ajís are fruity.","Sem descrição publicada encontrada.":"No published description found.","Ceviche, salsas frescas, molhos tipo ají; secar e moer.":"Ceviche, fresh salsas, ají-style sauces; dry and grind.","Espécie deduzida do nome 'Aji'.":"Species inferred from the name 'Aji'.","Itália (segundo o vendedor); parente da Jigsaw.":"Italy (according to the seller); a relative of Jigsaw.","1.500.000+ (vendedor, sem teste oficial).":"1,500,000+ (seller, no official test).","Sabor forte e terroso; ardor rápido que atinge o pico e passa.":"Strong, earthy flavour; fast heat that peaks and fades.","Volumosa, rugosa e com covinhas, ~7,5 cm. Verde, madura amarelo-mostarda.":"Hefty, wrinkled and dimpled, ~7.5 cm. Green, mustard-yellow when ripe.","Colhida verde dá ótimo molho picante verde; em gotas sobre pizza; molhos picantes.":"Picked green it makes a great green hot sauce; by the drop on pizza; hot sauces.","'Rawit' é o nome indonésio da pimenta tipo bird's eye.":"'Rawit' is the Indonesian name for bird's eye-type chillies.","Tipo bird's eye / tailandesa: 50.000–100.000.":"Bird's eye / Thai type: 50,000–100,000.","Muito mais picante do que o tamanho sugere.":"Far hotter than its size suggests.","Pequena e fina, vermelha ou verde.":"Small and thin, red or green.","Sambal, caris, salteados no wok, inteira em caldos, piri-piri.":"Sambal, curries, wok stir-fries, whole in broths, piri-piri.","'Rawit' é o nome indonésio das pimentas tipo bird's eye; os dados seguem esse tipo.":"'Rawit' is the Indonesian name for bird's eye-type chillies; the data follow that type.","Sem referências publicadas fiáveis.":"No reliable published references.","Scotch Bonnet laranja (lanterna)":"Orange Scotch Bonnet (lantern)","Caraíbas; símbolo da cozinha jamaicana.":"Caribbean; a symbol of Jamaican cooking.","Mais doce que o habanero; frutada, por vezes cítrica.":"Sweeter than habanero; fruity, sometimes citrusy.","Lanterna achatada, laranja.":"Flattened lantern, orange.","Essencial na cozinha jamaicana: marinadas jerk, molhos de pimenta, sopas, estufados e caris (frango jerk, caril de cabrito, peixe escovitch, camarão apimentado, arroz com feijão). Usada também nas cozinhas da África Ocidental, Sri Lanka e Maldivas.":"Essential in Jamaican cooking: jerk marinades, pepper sauces, soups, stews and curries (jerk chicken, curry goat, escovitch fish, pepper shrimp, rice and peas). Also used in West African, Sri Lankan and Maldivian cooking.","Linha 7 Pot Bubblegum, atribuída a Jon Harper (Reino Unido, c. 2011–2012). 'Frankenstein': sem dados.":"7 Pot Bubblegum line, attributed to Jon Harper (United Kingdom, c. 2011–2012). 'Frankenstein': no data.","7 Pot Bubblegum: ~1.000.000 estimado, sem teste oficial. 'Frankenstein': sem dados.":"7 Pot Bubblegum: ~1,000,000 estimated, no official test. 'Frankenstein': no data.","Frutado e citrino, por vezes lembra pastilha elástica.":"Fruity and citrusy, sometimes reminiscent of bubblegum.","BBG7: pequena e rugosa, com cálice grande que fica vermelho ('bleeding calyx').":"BBG7: small and wrinkled, with a large calyx that turns red ('bleeding calyx').","Inteira (sem pé) a ferver em estufados ou chili e retirada no fim: dá sabor com menos ardor. Picada para mais ardor. Molho picante; pó (moer ao ar livre).":"Whole (stem off), simmered in stews or chilli and removed at the end: flavour with less burn. Chopped for more heat. Hot sauce; powder (grind outdoors).","Bélgica (Laurent Minet): Bishop's Crown × Aji Fantasy.":"Belgium (Laurent Minet): Bishop's Crown × Aji Fantasy.","Médio ('moderado' segundo o criador); sem valor publicado.":"Medium ('moderate' according to the breeder); no published value.","Frutado vivo, levemente doce.":"Bright and fruity, lightly sweet.","Larga, 3 lóbulos, 5–6 cm. Verde, depois creme e laranja com riscas vermelhas tipo zebra.":"Wide, 3-lobed, 5–6 cm. Green, then cream and orange with zebra-like red stripes.","Fresca às rodelas, salsas e molhos.":"Fresh in slices, salsas and sauces.","Linha NuMex (Novo México, EUA).":"NuMex line (New Mexico, USA).","80.000 segundo o vendedor (Sandia Seed). Muito acima do jalapeño comum (2.500–10.000).":"80,000 according to the seller (Sandia Seed). Far above the common jalapeño (2,500–10,000).","Bom verde e maduro.":"Good green or ripe.","Jalapeño laranja vivo, ~6 cm, carne grossa.":"Bright orange jalapeño, ~6 cm, thick-fleshed.","Poppers recheados, pickles, salsas e molhos; boa verde ou laranja.":"Stuffed poppers, pickles, salsas and sauces; good green or orange.","Peppadew laranja":"Orange Peppadew","África do Sul (Eastern Cape, Limpopo).":"South Africa (Eastern Cape, Limpopo).","A Wikipedia não indica valor. Costuma ser citado à volta de 1.200 (não verificado).":"Wikipedia gives no value. Usually quoted at around 1,200 (not verified).","Doce e ligeiramente picante.":"Sweet and slightly hot.","Pequena e redonda, tipo cereja.":"Small and round, cherry-like.","Vende-se sobretudo em conserva doce-ácida. Recheada com queijo creme ou feta; saladas, pizza, tábuas de petiscos, mac and cheese.":"Sold mostly as a sweet-sour pickle. Stuffed with cream cheese or feta; salads, pizza, sharing boards, mac and cheese.","FOX Peppers (EUA).":"FOX Peppers (USA).","Fox Ghost Gnarly Ruby: 1.000.000+ (vendedor).":"Fox Ghost Gnarly Ruby: 1,000,000+ (seller).","Sem descrição detalhada.":"No detailed description.","Frutos quase todos roxos antes de amadurecer para vermelho-rubi escuro. Rugosa.":"Fruits almost entirely purple before ripening to dark ruby red. Wrinkled.","Peru, onde é nativa.":"Peru, where it is native.","Frutado tropical, lembra ananás.":"Tropical fruit, reminiscent of pineapple.","Fina e pendente, 5–7 cm. Verde, madura amarela.":"Thin and pendant, 5–7 cm. Green, yellow when ripe.","Sobretudo fresca: salsas tropicais e molhos picantes, saladas de fruta, sanduíches. Combina com carnes salgadas como presunto e bacon.":"Mostly fresh: tropical salsas and hot sauces, fruit salads, sandwiches. Pairs with salty meats such as cured ham and bacon.","Sem valor próprio. Linha FOX superhot (~1.000.000+).":"No value of its own. FOX superhot line (~1,000,000+).","Espera-se fruto escuro/roxo em verde que amadurece para laranja. Forma naga.":"Expected dark/purple fruit when green, ripening to orange. Naga shape.","Drax Diego (Itália).":"Drax Diego (Italy).","1.000.000+ (vendedor).":"1,000,000+ (seller).","Pêssego-laranja, textura muito rugosa, tipo cérebro.":"Peach-orange, very bumpy, brain-like texture.","Linha Sugar Rush criada na Finlândia (c. 2010), desenvolvida no País de Gales; as riscas surgiram nos EUA em 2015.":"Sugar Rush line created in Finland (c. 2010), developed in Wales; the stripes appeared in the USA in 2015.","25.000–50.000 (estimativa publicada).":"25,000–50,000 (published estimate).","Doce, estaladiça e bastante picante.":"Sweet, crunchy and fairly hot.","10–13 cm, ondulada. Pêssego-claro, madura laranja forte com riscas vermelhas.":"10–13 cm, wavy. Pale peach, ripening to deep orange with red stripes.","Molho picante, pickles (mesmo antes de ganhar cor), secar inteira ou em pó.":"Hot sauce, pickles (even before it colours), dried whole or as powder.","Linha Aji Flor Morado.":"Aji Flor Morado line.","'Picante' segundo o vendedor; sem valor publicado.":"'Hot' according to the seller; no published value.","Frutado vivo, quase citrino. Picante rápido e limpo.":"Bright and fruity, almost citrus. Quick, clean heat.","Fina, com riscas laranja e vermelhas. Flores roxas.":"Slender, with orange and red stripes. Purple flowers.","Marisco, peixe branco, vinagretes, molhos cítricos, salsas frescas, frango e legumes.":"Shellfish, white fish, vinaigrettes, citrus sauces, fresh salsas, chicken and vegetables.","Itália (Rocco Maltesi): 7 Pot Bubblegum × Jay's Peach Ghost Scorpion.":"Italy (Rocco Maltesi): 7 Pot Bubblegum × Jay's Peach Ghost Scorpion.","Perto de 1.000.000 (reportado).":"Close to 1,000,000 (reported).","Toranja e citrinos no início, meio floral, final terroso e doce.":"Grapefruit and citrus at first, floral middle, earthy-sweet finish.","Muito empolada e retorcida, 5–7 cm, laranja-escuro, cauda curta.":"Heavily blistered and twisted, 5–7 cm, deep orange, short tail.","Molhos fermentados ou de vinagre, óleos picantes, fumar.":"Fermented or vinegar sauces, chilli oils, smoking.","Brasil. Provável cruzamento natural de C. annuum com C. chinense.":"Brazil. Probably a natural cross of C. annuum and C. chinense.","Ligeiramente amarga, com notas florais. O sumo é roxo.":"Slightly bitter, with floral notes. The juice is purple.","Roxo quase preto, 5–7 cm. Não muda de cor ao amadurecer; só o interior passa de verde a roxo.":"Purple, almost black, 5–7 cm. It does not change colour when ripe; only the inside turns from green to purple.","Vale sobretudo pela cor: molhos e conservas roxas. Muito decorativa e base de vários cruzamentos (Black Panther, Purple Reaper e outros).":"Valued mainly for its colour: purple sauces and pickles. Very decorative and the basis of several crosses (Black Panther, Purple Reaper and others).","Cruzamento desconhecido.":"Unknown cross.","'Ao nível da ghost' segundo o vendedor; pode ainda ser instável.":"'Ghost-level' according to the seller; may still be unstable.","Laranja brilhante com manchas roxo-escuras a pretas.":"Bright orange with dark purple to black blotches.","Molhos em doses mínimas. Planta e frutos muito decorativos.":"Sauces in tiny doses. Very decorative plant and fruit.","Na fotografia: roxo-escuro, liso e cónico.":"In the photograph: dark purple, smooth and conical.","Nome genérico; sem referências publicadas.":"Generic name; no published references.","Itália (Giancarlo 'Faddas' Fadda): Chupetinho White × Reaper Pink.":"Italy (Giancarlo 'Faddas' Fadda): Chupetinho White × Reaper Pink.","Superhot segundo o criador; sem valor publicado.":"Superhot according to the breeder; no published value.","Frutada e doce, final ácido.":"Fruity and sweet, tangy finish.","Pêssego a roxo-claro, curvas suaves, por vezes cauda torcida.":"Peach to pale purple, smooth curves, sometimes a twisted tail.","Molhos e salsas, fresca em quantidades mínimas.":"Sauces and salsas, fresh in tiny amounts.","Médio (3 em 10 na escala do vendedor); sem valor SHU.":"Medium (3 out of 10 on the seller's scale); no SHU value.","Muito frutado ('melocotón' é pêssego).":"Very fruity ('melocotón' means peach).","Verde-claro, madura amarelo-alaranjada.":"Light green, ripening to yellow-orange.","Molhos, pó amarelo aromático, fresca.":"Sauces, aromatic yellow powder, fresh.","Itália, segundo um dos vendedores.":"Italy, according to one seller.","10.000–15.000 (vendedor).":"10,000–15,000 (seller).","Frutado, com final ligeiramente floral.":"Fruity, with a slightly floral finish.","Creme/branca quando madura, forma invulgar. Planta vigorosa (80–120 cm), precisa de tutor.":"Cream/white when ripe, unusual shape. Vigorous plant (80–120 cm) that needs staking.","Saladas e salsas frescas; também seca bem.":"Fresh salads and salsas; also dries well.","Bolívia.":"Bolivia.","Suave a médio (vendedor); sem valor SHU.":"Mild to medium (seller); no SHU value.","Estaladiça, frutada e doce.":"Crunchy, fruity and sweet.","Cerca de 4 × 2,5 cm. Verde, depois laranja e vermelha.":"About 4 × 2.5 cm. Green, then orange and red.","Fresca, petisco, molhos, pó, pickles.":"Fresh, as a snack, sauces, powder, pickles.","Mutação branca da Aji Fantasy (Finlândia).":"White mutation of Aji Fantasy (Finland).","Suave a médio (vendedor); o picante está no centro.":"Mild to medium (seller); the heat is in the centre.","Fresca e limpa; menos doce que a Aji Fantasy amarela.":"Fresh and clean; less sweet than the yellow Aji Fantasy.","Branca, em forma de sino, carne grossa. Planta compacta.":"White, bell-shaped, thick-fleshed. Compact plant.","Recheada; usar como pimento doce. Tirando o centro, quase não pica.":"Stuffed; use like a sweet pepper. With the centre removed it is barely hot.","Cultivar ornamental.":"Ornamental cultivar.","45.000 (vendedor).":"45,000 (seller).","Picante; sem descrição detalhada.":"Hot; no detailed description.","Tipo azeitona, 2,5–5 cm. Roxa, madura vermelha. Folhas e flores arroxeadas.":"Olive-shaped, 2.5–5 cm. Purple, red when ripe. Purplish leaves and flowers.","Fresca, salsas, saladas, molhos, pickles. Excelente em vaso.":"Fresh, salsas, salads, sauces, pickles. Excellent in a pot.","Equador e Peru.":"Ecuador and Peru.","Frutada e cítrica, com notas marcadas de erva-príncipe quando madura. Ardor direto que passa depressa.":"Fruity and citrusy, with marked lemongrass notes when ripe. Direct heat that fades quickly.","Fina e cónica, 8–10 cm, direita ou ligeiramente curva. Verde, madura amarelo vivo.":"Slender and conical, 8–10 cm, straight or slightly curved. Green, bright yellow when ripe.","Fresca e sem sementes em salsa, ceviche e sopas; marisco, arroz, aves e salteados (muito usada em pratos tailandeses). Pickles, molho picante e geleia; seca e moída para temperos.":"Fresh and deseeded in salsa, ceviche and soups; seafood, rice, poultry and stir-fries (widely used in Thai dishes). Pickles, hot sauce and jelly; dried and ground for seasonings.","Etiópia e Eritreia; descende de pimentas levadas pelos portugueses nos séc. XV–XVI.":"Ethiopia and Eritrea; descends from chillies brought by the Portuguese in the 15th–16th centuries.","Sumarenta, fumada, com acidez frutada. O ardor sobe devagar.":"Juicy and smoky, with fruity acidity. The heat builds slowly.","Fina e cónica, 10–15 cm, com pregas e rugas. Verde, madura castanho-chocolate avermelhado.":"Slender and conical, 10–15 cm, with folds and wrinkles. Green, ripening to reddish chocolate brown.","Principal ingrediente do berbere (com feno-grego, cardamomo, gengibre, pimenta-da-jamaica): doro wot (estufado de frango) com injera, e awaze (molho com alho e vinho). Também fresca em saladas e marinadas, cozinhada em sopas, estufados, feijão e assados, ou em pó para rubs e molhos de churrasco.":"Main ingredient of berbere (with fenugreek, cardamom, ginger, allspice): doro wot (chicken stew) with injera, and awaze (sauce with garlic and wine). Also fresh in salads and marinades, cooked in soups, stews, beans and roasts, or as powder for rubs and barbecue sauces.","Brasil. O nome vem de Werner Mathi, que a descreveu; chama-se 'trepadeira' apesar de a planta ser compacta.":"Brazil. Named after Werner Mathi, who described it; called 'trepadeira' (climber) although the plant is compact.","5.000–15.000 (vendedor); outra fonte indica ~5.000.":"5,000–15,000 (seller); another source gives ~5,000.","Muito frutada e equilibrada; quem a provou fala em pêssego, frutos vermelhos ou ananás. Ardor imediato que passa em poucos minutos.":"Very fruity and balanced; tasters mention peach, red berries or pineapple. Immediate heat that fades within minutes.","Redonda tipo cereja, 2–3 cm, pele lisa. Branca, depois amarela, laranja e vermelho-batom.":"Round, cherry-like, 2–3 cm, smooth skin. White, then yellow, orange and lipstick red.","Fresca, cozinhada, em conserva, em saladas e em molho picante.":"Fresh, cooked, pickled, in salads and in hot sauce.","Norte do Peru; cresce sobretudo em estado selvagem e só há pouco é cultivada comercialmente.":"Northern Peru; grows mostly wild and has only recently been cultivated commercially.","Doce e frutada: a fruta do habanero com muito menos ardor.":"Sweet and fruity: the fruitiness of habanero with far less heat.","Minúscula e redonda (~6 mm, do tamanho de uma ervilha). Verde, madura amarela.":"Tiny and round (~6 mm, the size of a pea). Green, yellow when ripe.","Tempero de acabamento: espremer a fresco sobre arroz, peixe ou frango para soltar o sumo. Também em salsas e molhos; combina com fruta tropical.":"Finishing spice: squeeze fresh over rice, fish or chicken to release the juice. Also in salsas and sauces; pairs with tropical fruit.","Aribibi, Amazónia boliviana. Também vendida como Aji Gusanito, Aji Gusano, Caterpillar e Turtle Claw.":"Aribibi, Bolivian Amazon. Also sold as Aji Gusanito, Aji Gusano, Caterpillar and Turtle Claw.","As fontes divergem: ~96.000 (Turtle Claw, Sea Spring Seeds), ~150.000 (estimativa de um provador), 300.000–470.000 (Garden Hoard).":"Sources differ: ~96,000 (Turtle Claw, Sea Spring Seeds), ~150,000 (a taster's estimate), 300,000–470,000 (Garden Hoard).","Muito perfumada: notas cítricas e doces, amadeiradas, com fundo de baunilha; o cheiro espalha-se pela casa ao cortar. Outra fonte fala em sabor a limão.":"Very perfumed: citrus and sweet woody notes with a vanilla-like background; the smell fills the house when cut. Another source mentions a lemon flavour.","Fina, rugosa e retorcida, tipo lagarta, até ~3 cm. Verde-claro, madura amarelo-marfim.":"Thin, wrinkled and twisted, caterpillar-like, up to ~3 cm. Light green, ivory-yellow when ripe.","Fácil de dosear pelo tamanho: 2–3 frutos chegam para 1,5 kg de chili con carne. Salsas, molhos, estufados, salteados; seca bem. Há quem a use em chocolate quente.":"Easy to dose thanks to its size: 2–3 fruits are enough for 1.5 kg of chili con carne. Salsas, sauces, stews, stir-fries; dries well. Some use it in hot chocolate.","Aji Gusanito, Turtle Claw e Caterpillar aparecem como sinónimos em várias fontes; a Sea Spring Seeds diz apenas que são parecidas. As duas fotografias podem ser seleções diferentes.":"Aji Gusanito, Turtle Claw and Caterpillar appear as synonyms in several sources; Sea Spring Seeds only says they look alike. The two photographs may be different selections.","Cultivada sobretudo no Sudeste Asiático (Tailândia, Indonésia). A espécie é americana e chegou à Ásia nos séculos XVI–XVII.":"Grown mainly in Southeast Asia (Thailand, Indonesia). The species is American and reached Asia in the 16th–17th centuries.","Ardor intenso e persistente, com sabor frutado (muito apreciado na Tailândia).":"Intense, lingering heat with a fruity flavour (much prized in Thailand).","Pequena, fina e pontiaguda (1–7 cm). Verde, madura vermelha.":"Small, thin and pointed (1–7 cm). Green, red when ripe.","Na Tailândia: caris e saladas, verde ou madura, e crua a acompanhar pratos como khao kha mu. Na Indonésia: sambal, e inteira a acompanhar fritos. Serve para piri-piri caseiro em azeite (a piri-piri africana é parente próxima, C. frutescens, com ardor parecido).":"In Thailand: curries and salads, green or ripe, and raw alongside dishes such as khao kha mu. In Indonesia: sambal, and whole alongside fried snacks. Works for homemade piri-piri in olive oil (African piri-piri is a close relative, C. frutescens, with similar heat).","Tailândia (pelo nome; o vendedor não confirma a origem).":"Thailand (from the name; the seller does not confirm the origin).","Sem descrição própria; as bird's eye são frutadas e muito picantes.":"No description of its own; bird's eye chillies are fruity and very hot.","Fonte: pequena, fina e pontiaguda (1–2 cm), branco-amarelada e brilhante quando madura. Muito produtiva.":"Source: small, thin and pointed (1–2 cm), glossy yellowish-white when ripe. Very productive.","Carne fina: boa para cozinha rápida no wok e para secar.":"Thin flesh: good for quick wok cooking and for drying.","As fontes descrevem a White Thai como branca quando madura; o fruto fotografado é vermelho.":"Sources describe White Thai as white when ripe; the fruit in the photograph is red.","Chiltepín":"Chiltepín","Silvestre, do sul da América do Norte ao norte da América do Sul. A colheita comercial faz-se sobretudo em Sonora (México), em plantas selvagens. Pimenta nativa oficial do Texas desde 1997 e provável antepassada do C. annuum domesticado.":"Wild, from southern North America to northern South America. Commercial harvest is mainly in Sonora (Mexico), from wild plants. Official native pepper of Texas since 1997 and probable ancestor of domesticated C. annuum.","Ardor 'arrebatado': intenso mas curto (o pequín, parente, é mais lento e duradouro).":"'Arrebatado' heat: intense but short (its relative the pequín is slower and longer-lasting).","Minúscula, redonda a ligeiramente oval (~8 mm). Vermelha a vermelho-alaranjada.":"Tiny, round to slightly oval (~8 mm). Red to orange-red.","Verde em vinagre (a forma mais picante) ou seca ao sol e esmagada à mesa. Sem sementes perde ardor. O picante varia com a chuva do ano: anos secos dão frutos mais fracos.":"Green in vinegar (the hottest form) or sun-dried and crushed at the table. Deseeded it loses heat. The heat varies with the year's rainfall: dry years give weaker fruit.","Origem desconhecida; cultivada sobretudo no leste do Texas, na Luisiana e em partes do México.":"Origin unknown; grown mainly in East Texas, Louisiana and parts of Mexico.","Forma fálica, daí o nome. Vermelha ou amarela.":"Phallic shape, hence the name. Red or yellow.","Pickles, salsa e chili; substitui jalapeño ou serrano.":"Pickles, salsa and chilli; a substitute for jalapeño or serrano.","Cultivar brasileira.":"Brazilian cultivar.","Picante mas variável. O vendedor não dá valor porque as estimativas publicadas divergem muito.":"Hot but variable. The seller gives no value because published estimates differ widely.","Fragrância frutada e aromática; sabor levemente doce e frutado, depois o ardor.":"Fruity, aromatic fragrance; lightly sweet and fruity flavour, then the heat.","Pequena e pendente, tipo lanterna com bico. Quase preta, depois roxa, rosa e por fim pêssego; várias cores na mesma planta.":"Small and pendant, lantern-shaped with a point. Almost black, then purple, pink and finally peach; several colours on the same plant.","Salsa cozinhada (tomate, cebola, alho, lima, coentros), molho picante, chutney e marinadas cozinhadas. Começar com pouco.":"Cooked salsa (tomato, onion, garlic, lime, coriander), hot sauce, chutney and cooked marinades. Start with a little.","Variante natural castanha da Carolina Reaper (EUA).":"Natural brown variant of the Carolina Reaper (USA).","2.200.000 segundo o vendedor; sem medição própria publicada.":"2,200,000 according to the seller; no published measurement of its own.","Sem descrição própria. Nas ghost e nos habaneros, as variantes chocolate são mais terrosas e fumadas.":"No description of its own. In ghosts and habaneros, chocolate variants are earthier and smokier.","Castanho-chocolate, rugosa, com cauda.":"Chocolate brown, wrinkled, with a tail.","A cor escura serve molhos de churrasco e mole. Usar em quantidades mínimas: molhos (de vinagre, doces ou fumados), pó para dosear à pitada, óleo picante. Tirar a placenta branca reduz o ardor; assar antes suaviza. Luvas e cuidado com os olhos.":"The dark colour suits barbecue sauces and mole. Use in tiny amounts: sauces (vinegar-based, sweet or smoky), powder to dose by the pinch, chilli oil. Removing the white placenta reduces the heat; roasting first softens it. Gloves, and mind your eyes.","Na fotografia: forma de Reaper com cauda, laranja-avermelhada com zonas roxas.":"In the photograph: Reaper shape with a tail, reddish orange with purple patches.","Sem referências publicadas; pela forma, parece derivada da Carolina Reaper.":"No published references; by its shape it seems to derive from the Carolina Reaper.","Na fotografia: laranja com zonas roxas, muito irregular.":"In the photograph: orange with purple patches, very irregular.","O fruto fotografado é mais curto e largo do que o habitual nesta variedade.":"The photographed fruit is shorter and wider than is usual for this variety.","O fruto fotografado está vermelho (maduro).":"The photographed fruit is red (ripe).","Os frutos fotografados são um pouco pontiagudos; o chiltepín costuma ser redondo.":"The photographed fruits are slightly pointed; chiltepín is usually round.","EUA, segundo o vendedor.":"USA, according to the seller.","15.000–30.000 (vendedor).":"15,000–30,000 (seller).","Verdes, sabem a pimento; roxas e vermelhas ganham picante a sério (vendedor).":"Green, they taste of bell pepper; purple and red, they get properly hot (seller).","Ovais, eretas, cerca de 1 × 3 cm; passam de verde a roxo e vermelho. Folhagem verde-escura a roxa, flores violeta, planta com cerca de 60 cm. Na fotografia: quatro frutos cónicos, do roxo ao laranja e ao vermelho.":"Oval, upright, about 1 × 3 cm; they turn from green to purple and red. Dark green to purple foliage, violet flowers, plant about 60 cm. In the photo: four conical fruits, from purple to orange and red.","O vendedor indica-a para molhos picantes, pastas de malagueta e para secar. Os frutos verdes comem-se e sabem a pimento.":"The seller recommends it for hot sauces, chilli pastes and drying. The green fruits are edible and taste of bell pepper.","Dados de uma única fonte (vendedor).":"Data from a single source (seller).","A Murupi anda pelos 100.000 SHU (vendedor); esta forma escura não tem valor próprio publicado.":"Murupi runs at about 100,000 SHU (seller); this dark form has no published value of its own.","Por identificar":"To be identified","Por identificar. Pode ser a Big Red Mama (linha Big Mama, superhot, 750.000–1.000.000 SHU segundo a Pepper Joe's) ou o pimento doce 'Big Red'. Falta confirmar no pacote.":"To be identified. It may be Big Red Mama (Big Mama line, superhot, 750,000–1,000,000 SHU according to Pepper Joe's) or the 'Big Red' sweet pepper. Still to be checked on the seed packet.","Por identificar: não há referências publicadas com este nome. Falta confirmar no pacote.":"To be identified: there are no published references under this name. Still to be checked on the seed packet.","A Wikipedia indica 1.177 SHU; a PepperScale, 1.100–1.200.":"Wikipedia gives 1,177 SHU; PepperScale, 1,100–1,200.","Valor da Aji Fantasy (5.000–10.000, PepperScale). A branca é descrita como suave a média; o picante está no centro.":"Value for Aji Fantasy (5,000–10,000, PepperScale). The white one is described as mild to medium; the heat sits in the core.","Provavelmente a Pockmark Orange: Austrália (Jason Richards), Bhut Jolokia × Pimenta da Neyde.":"Probably Pockmark Orange: Australia (Jason Richards), Bhut Jolokia × Pimenta da Neyde.","Pockmark Orange: 1.000.000–2.000.000, estimativa do vendedor.":"Pockmark Orange: 1,000,000–2,000,000, seller's estimate.","Frutada, com notas de pêssego e citrinos e um fundo floral e fumado (descrição da Pockmark).":"Fruity, with notes of peach and citrus over a floral, smoky base (description of Pockmark).","Na fotografia: laranja com zonas roxas, muito irregular. A Pockmark nasce roxo-escura e acaba laranja picotada com manchas roxas.":"In the photo: orange with purple patches, very irregular. Pockmark starts dark purple and ends up a pitted orange with purple blushes.","Molhos de fruta (manga, ananás) e pó, em doses mínimas. Luvas e cuidado com os olhos.":"Fruit sauces (mango, pineapple) and powder, in tiny doses. Gloves, and keep it away from your eyes.","Identificação provável: o nome e a fotografia batem com a Pockmark Orange. Falta confirmar no pacote.":"Probable identification: the name and the photo match Pockmark Orange. Still to be checked on the seed packet.","PepperScale: 60.000–80.000. Outras estimativas publicadas divergem.":"PepperScale: 60,000–80,000. Other published estimates differ.","10.000–30.000 segundo a The Hippy Seed Company.":"10,000–30,000 according to The Hippy Seed Company."}};
